<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">3.RML  and subsidiaries  are engaged in the manufacture of components for Transportation industry, which in the context of Ind AS 108 – OS, is considered as the only operating segment of the Grp. 4. During the yr ended Mar 31, 21, the Co had assessed the carrying value of its investments in a subsidiary and considered the fair value changes thereto resulting in a reduction in the carrying value aggregating to Rs. 62.50 cr being shown as an exceptional item for the yr ended Mar 31, 21. In order to carry out the above assessment, projections of future cash flows of the operating SDS based on the most recent long-term forecasts, including selling price as well as volumes are estimated over the next 5 yrs. The estimation of sales volumes is based on mgmt's assessment of probability of securing the new businesses in the future, adverse business impact and uncertainties arising due to COVID-19 pandemic to the extent known. The impact of COVID-19 on the Co’s FR may differ from that estimated as at the DOA of these FR depending on the circumstances that may evolve in the future.5. The Co’s subsidiary in the U.S LMCA was entitled to certain economic relief provided by the U.S government in order to manage the impact of COVID-19 pandemic. Pursuant to such economic relief schemes, during the 9 months ended Dec 31, 21, LMCA received an approval for forgiveness of the PPP Loan from the U.S. SBA for an amt of USD 2.63 million (INR 19.45 crores). Further, LMCA  was eligible for ERC, from the U.S. IRS during the 9 months ended Dec 31, 21 for an amount of USD 3.66 million (INR 27.26 crores) for the qtr ended Dec 31, 21 and USD 1.23 million (INR 9.14 crores) for the qtr ended Sep 30, 21). The agg amts of such relief have been recorded as an exceptional income in the consol results for the qtr ended Sep 30,21 and for the qtr and 9 months ended De 31, 2021. 6. Pursuant to the BTA dated Oct 11, 21, the Co acquired the SCB of YTPL for an agg consideration of INR 23.19 crores on a slump sale basis effective from Oct 31, 21. Pursuant to such acquisition, the Property, P and E, Intangibles, Inv and other nca relating to SCB have been transferred to the Co.7. COVID-19 pandemic has rapidly spread throughout the world, including Ind. Govt have taken significant measures to curb the spread of the virus including imposing mandatory lockdowns and restrictions on activities. Consequently, the Cos mfg plants and offices had to operate under restrictions for a period of time during the 9 months ended Dec 31,21. These measures have an impact on matters relating to commodity prices, SCM, customer demand, personnel available for work and for being available to access offices etc. The Co/Grp has considered the possible effects that may result from the continued effect of the pandemic on the carrying amounts of assets, capital and financial resources, profitability, liquidity position, internal financial controls etc. In developing the assumptions relating to the possible future uncertainties, the co/ Grp, as at the date of approval of these FR has used internal and external sources of information and based on current estimates expects that the carrying amount of these assets will be recovered. The impact of COVID-19 on the Cos/Grps FR may differ from that estimated as at the date of approval of these financial results depending on the circumstances that may evolve in the future. The Co/Grp will continue to closely monitor any material changes to future economic conditions. Subsequent to the qtr ended Dec 31 21, the Co has received Rs.15 crores from RHL as warrant exercise price towards conversion of the outstanding 8,49,979 warrants issued on PB and has allotted equivalent eq shares of Rs.10 each fully paid up on Jan 11, 22. Consequently, the issued and paid up capital stands increased by 8,49,979 eq shares of Rs.10 each fully paid-up towards which listing approvals were received on Jan 18, 22 from NSE/BSE &amp; trading approvals are awaited from BSE and NSE</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
